// expect-error: T225
// Z3 corpus #55: axis-1 — Wall 4 Step 7 return refinement violation.
//
// WHAT THIS FIXTURE PROVES
//
// The rejecting counterpart of fixture 54. `fn bad() -> i64 where @ > 0`
// declares the return value must be `> 0`. The body's `return 0;` Z3-
// fails on `not(0 > 0)`, and T225 fires at the return statement.
//
// Per N25-S7 the check fires at every `return <expr>` in the function
// body (including those nested inside `if`/`match`/`while`/`for`/blocks)
// via the recursive walker baked into `check_return`. Per N15-S7 the
// check is ADDITIVE on top of the existing `type_compatible` check at
// the same site.
//
// THE LANGUAGE PRIMITIVES THIS NEEDED
//
//   * Step 7 `tracker.current_return_refinement` set by
//     `check_function_block` at fn entry.
//   * Step 7 `check_return` body-level dispatch to T225.
//
// MUTATION CONTRACT
//
// The MUTATION_SITE is the entire single-line `fn bad` declaration.
// Removing the line removes the violating function and leaves a
// compiling program (just the entry actor).
module sigil;

fn bad() -> i64 where @ > 0 { return 0; }  // MUTATION_SITE

entry actor Main {
    on Tick() -> i64 {
        return 1;
    }
}
